and I think there are actually two or three that come to mind.

00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:26.060
Two or three groups.

00:45:26.060 --> 00:45:27.480
One being

00:45:27.480 --> 00:45:28.880
if you are involved,

00:45:28.880 --> 00:45:30.835
if you're a research coordinator,

00:45:30.835 --> 00:45:33.480
and you want to do actually more,

00:45:33.480 --> 00:45:35.620
not just recruit patients and help with

00:45:35.620 --> 00:45:38.675
the day to day functions of a clinic or a lab

00:45:38.675 --> 00:45:43.075
then having these skills you can be more involved

00:45:43.075 --> 00:45:45.350
and assist the PI

00:45:45.350 --> 00:45:48.620
in actually helping them develop protocols as well as

00:45:48.620 --> 00:45:52.545
setting up databases and even helping with statistical analysis,

00:45:52.545 --> 00:45:56.660
and to look at sort of preliminary data and so on.

00:45:56.660 --> 00:45:58.545
That's one area.

00:45:58.545 --> 00:46:02.030
Another area is if you come from the writing world,

00:46:02.030 --> 00:46:04.140
Medical Science journals

00:46:04.140 --> 00:46:06.940
this would of course be immensely helpful.

00:46:06.940 --> 00:46:11.485
